##  Pinged across the WireGuard tunnel and captured the encrypted UDP traffic to confirm no plaintext is visible

> **Timestamp:** `2026-07-07 15:48:45`

### 01. `sudo timeout 6 tcpdump -i lo udp port 51820 -A -c 5 > /tmp/wg_capture.txt & sleep 2`

```bash
sudo timeout 6 tcpdump -i lo udp port 51820 -A -c 5 > /tmp/wg_capture.txt & sleep 2
```

**Output:**

```text
tcpdump: verbose output suppressed, use -v[v]... for full protocol decode
listening on lo, link-type EN10MB (Ethernet), snapshot length 262144 bytes
```

### 02. `ping -c 3 10.200.0.2`

```bash
ping -c 3 10.200.0.2
```

**Output:**

```text
PING 10.200.0.2 (10.200.0.2) 56(84) bytes of data.
64 bytes from 10.200.0.2: icmp_seq=1 ttl=64 time=0.838 ms
64 bytes from 10.200.0.2: icmp_seq=2 ttl=64 time=0.095 ms
64 bytes from 10.200.0.2: icmp_seq=3 ttl=64 time=0.110 ms

--- 10.200.0.2 ping statistics ---
3 packets transmitted, 3 received, 0% packet loss, time 2048ms
rtt min/avg/max/mdev = 0.095/0.347/0.838/0.346 ms
```

